+# Privacy and deployment
+
+This is a static, script-free website. Publish only `dist/`, generated by
+`npm run build`. No packages are installed to render or build the site.
+
+## Data and third-party inventory
+
+| Component | Browser data exposure | Decision |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| HTML, CSS, coffee photograph | Requests go to the site host | Keep local; no remote fonts, CDNs, image services, or embeds |
+| Original Unsplash photograph | None to Unsplash during browsing | Downloaded into `assets/coffee.jpg`; source: https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085 |
+| Analytics, advertising, tag managers | None; absent | Do not add by default |
+| Client JavaScript, cookies, browser storage | None; absent | CSP blocks scripts and outbound connections |
+| Forms, accounts, rewards, ordering, payments | Not implemented here | Existing navigation is a placeholder for services outside this repository |
+| Hosting provider | Connection information and requested paths; possible access logs | Operator must review the selected host and configure retention |
+| Development start command | `pnpm dlx statikk` downloads a development tool when explicitly run | Not part of the published site or build; no runtime dependency |
+
+This is a source audit, not a certification of a hosting provider or unimplemented
+services. No consent banner is needed for the current implementation because it
+does not offer optional tracking or browser storage. Adding collection changes
+that assessment and requires an updated notice before release.
+
+## Security headers
+
+`_headers` supplies response headers on static hosts that support that format,
+including Netlify and Cloudflare Pages. `netlify.toml` configures the build and
+publish directory for Netlify. For other hosts, translate `_headers` into their
+response-header configuration; serving this directory alone does not activate
+those headers. The existing development start command does not establish that
+production headers are active.
+
+The HTML also includes a fallback CSP and referrer policy. HTTP-only protections
+such as `frame-ancestors`, HSTS, Permissions-Policy, and anti-sniffing must be
+served as response headers. Serve production over HTTPS and redirect HTTP to
+HTTPS at the host. HSTS applies to this hostname only; subdomains have not been
+assumed to support HTTPS. Configure the host/CDN to honor `Cache-Control: no-store`
+and avoid injecting analytics or other scripts. Before release, verify the actual
+production responses, including the privacy page, redirects, and error pages,
+carry the intended policies. No deployment or live header verification has been
+performed by this change.
+
+The CSP allows local images and styles and denies scripts, connections, forms,
+frames, plugins, workers, and unlisted resources. Keep secrets, customer data,
+and build configuration outside the published directory. The build uses an
+explicit allowlist to avoid shipping these accidentally.
+
+## Minimization and secure handling
+
+The current site collects no application data, stores no identifiers, and has no
+client-side personal data to retain or delete. The privacy notice distinguishes
+that behavior from host access logs. Configure host logs to exclude unnecessary
+query strings, cookies, and request bodies; restrict access, select the shortest
+operational retention period, and document it once the host is chosen. Do not
+put personal information in URLs, analytics, console logs, or browser storage.
+
+Before implementing accounts or ordering, define required fields and purposes,
+retention and deletion rules, and user contact procedures. Implement validation
+and authorization on the server, use secure HttpOnly SameSite session cookies,
+and require CSRF protection for state-changing requests (including logout).
+Do not make the existing GET logout link perform a state change. Card data
+should be handled by a reviewed payment provider rather than stored here.
+
+## Reviewing future changes
+
+Run `npm test` and `npm run build` before release. `npm run audit:privacy` runs
+the standalone source audit. The build fails if that audit fails. Regression
+tests exercise tracking pixels, outbound URLs, scripts, forms, inline handlers,
+CSS requests, and weakened markup policies. The conservative checks cover this
+site's simple markup and CSS; they are not a general HTML parser or dependency
+vulnerability scanner.
+
+Before adding a dependency, remote resource, script, SDK, or collection feature:
+
+1. Establish why it is needed and whether a local or data-free approach works.
+2. Record the provider, exact data fields, endpoints, purpose, retention,
+   subprocessors, access controls, deletion process, and security review.
+3. Review the provider's actual documentation and contracts. Do not assume that
+   a lack of cookies means a service cannot track users.
+4. Update this inventory and the public notice; obtain consent before optional
+   collection where required. Honor refusal and withdrawal without loading the
+   optional service first.
+5. Add narrowly scoped policies and meaningful regression checks. Do not relax
+   CSP to wildcards, inline scripts, or arbitrary connections to pass the build.
+
+Repeat the inventory review on every integration change and before each release.
